isTight -- determine if toric quiver is tight
*********************************************

  * Usage: 
        isTight Q
        isTight(Q, W)
        isTight(W, Q)
        isTight(W, Q, Format => "Flow")
        isTight(W, Q, Format => "Weight")
  * Inputs:
      * Q, a *note toric quiver: ToricQuiver,, 
      * W, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Format => ..., default value "Flow", specify whether input W is a flow
        (integer values associated to each arrow) or the image of the flow
        under the map weights (integer values associated to each vertex).
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, true if the toric quiver
        is tight with respect to the specified flow, and false otherwise

Description
===========

A toric quiver $Q$ is tight with respect to a given flow if there is no maximal
unstable subquiver of codimension 1. That is, every unstable subquiver of $Q$
has at most $|Q_1|-2$ arrows. This method determines if a toric quiver $Q$ is
tight with respect to the vertex weights induced by its flow.

+----------------------------------+
|i1 : isTight bipartiteQuiver(2, 3)|
|                                  |
|o1 = true                         |
+----------------------------------+
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : isTight bipartiteQuiver(2, 3, Flow => "Random")|
|                                                    |
|o2 = false                                          |
+----------------------------------------------------+
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : isTight (bipartiteQuiver(2, 3), {2,1,2,3,2,3})|
|                                                   |
|o3 = true                                          |
+---------------------------------------------------+
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : isTight ({0,0,0,0,0,1}, bipartiteQuiver(2, 3))|
|                                                   |
|o4 = false                                         |
+---------------------------------------------------+

Ways to use isTight:
====================

  * "isTight(List,ToricQuiver)"
  * "isTight(ToricQuiver)"
  * "isTight(ToricQuiver,List)"

