makeTight -- return a tight quiver with the same flow polytope
**************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        makeTight(W, Q)
  * Inputs:
      * W, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of values corresponding to a
        weight on each arrow of Q
      * Q, a *note toric quiver: ToricQuiver,, 
  * Outputs:
      * Q, a *note toric quiver: ToricQuiver,, that is tight with respect to
        the flow on the input, and which has the same flow polytope as the
        input.

Description
===========

Let $\theta$ be an integral weight assigned to the vertices of a quiver $Q$.
The quiver $Q$ is called $\theta$-tight if for every arrow $\alpha$, the
subquiver $Q\setminus \alpha$ is $\theta$-stable. Every quiver can be tightened
by contraction of certain arrows in Q and changing the weight accordingly, see
Section 4 at Altmann, Klaus, and Duco van Straten. "Smoothing of quiver
varieties." manuscripta mathematica 129 (2009): 211-230. (see
https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00229-009-0255-6 )

+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : Q = bipartiteQuiver(2, 3);                         |
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : w = {-5,-1,2,2,2};                                 |
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : makeTight(w, Q)                                    |
|                                                        |
|o3 = ToricQuiver{flow => {0, -1, 1, 1}                 }|
|                 IncidenceMatrix => | -1 1  1  0  |     |
|                                    | 0  -1 -1 -1 |     |
|                                    | 1  0  0  1  |     |
|                 Q0 => {0, 1, 2}                        |
|                 Q1 => {{0, 2}, {1, 0}, {1, 0}, {1, 2}} |
|                 weights => {0, -1, 1}                  |
|                                                        |
|o3 : ToricQuiver                                        |
+--------------------------------------------------------+

