primitiveArrows -- list the primitive arrows in a quiver
********************************************************

  * Usage: 
        primitiveArrows Q
  * Inputs:
      * Q, a *note toric quiver: ToricQuiver,, 
  * Outputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of arrow indices corresponding to
        the primitive arrows in Q

Description
===========

This method returns a list of the arrows in the provided quiver that are
primitive. An arrow a=(v0,v1) in the quiver Q is primitive if there exists an
oriented non-empty path from v0 to v1 in Q that is distinct from a. Thus, if
the arrow a is primitive, then removing it from the quiver results in a quiver
that still contains a path between its endpoints v0 and v1.

+----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : primitiveArrows toricQuiver {{0,1},{0,2},{0,3},{1,2},{1,3},{2,3}}|
|                                                                      |
|o1 = {0, 3, 5}                                                        |
|                                                                      |
|o1 : List                                                             |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------+

