quiverWeights -- return the weight attribute associated to the toric quiver
***************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        quiverWeights Q
  * Inputs:
      * Q, a *note toric quiver: ToricQuiver,, 
  * Outputs:
      * W, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of the weights induced by the
        flow on the quiver

Description
===========

This method returns the weights of the provided toric quiver. The weights are
the image of the quiver flow under the inc map, which is defined as $$
\text{inc}(\mathbf{w})(i) := \sum_{a\in Q_1 \atop a^{+} = i} \mathbf{w}(a) -
\sum_{a\in Q_1 \atop a^{-} = i} \mathbf{w}(a) \quad \text{ for all } i \in Q_0.
$$ where for any arrow $a\in Q_1$, we denote its head as $a^{+} \in Q_0$ and
its tail as $a^{-} \in Q_0$.

+-------------------------------+
|i1 : Q = bipartiteQuiver(2, 3);|
+-------------------------------+
|i2 : quiverWeights Q           |
|                               |
|o2 = {-3, -3, 2, 2, 2}         |
|                               |
|o2 : List                      |
+-------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note ToricQuiver: ToricQuiver, -- the ToricQuiver datatype
  * *note incInverse: incInverse, -- compute a flow in the preimage for a given
    weight

